<Base title="Origins and Credits">
  <div class="content-wrap wiki-wrap">
    <div class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The people behind the adventure</p><h1>Origins & credits</h1><p>Grand Anthology would not exist without the creators who built the world beneath it.</p></div>
    <section class="panel"><h2>The foundation: Pokémon World</h2><p>This project extends <a href="https://github.com/evilchinesefood/PKMN-World">Pokémon World</a>, created by David A. (evilchinesefood) and contributors. The three-region integration, shared adventure, and substantial existing systems belong to that project and its upstream community.</p><p>The foundation also draws upon <a href="https://github.com/rh-hideout/pokeemerald-expansion">pokeemerald-expansion</a>, <a href="https://github.com/pret/pokeemerald">pret’s pokeemerald</a>, and work including <a href="https://github.com/PokemonHnS-Development/pokemonHnS">Pokémon Heart & Soul</a>. Refer to the complete historical acknowledgments, not this brief summary, for individual contributions.</p></section>
    <section class="panel"><h2>Grand Anthology</h2><p><strong>Creator and maintainer:</strong> Pranav Sarma (DevElectrum). <strong>AI development collaborator:</strong> Astra, powered by ChatGPT. The human maintainer guides decisions and project direction, while AI-assisted code and documentation require careful review and testing.</p><p>Project goals emphasize catching Pokémon, exploring the expanded world, building teams, and enjoying the adventure rather than mandatory punishing difficulty.</p></section>
    <section class="panel"><h2>Full attribution</h2><ul class="link-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/DevElectrum/grand-anthology/blob/main/CREDITS.md">Preserved original and expanded credits ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/DevElectrum/grand-anthology/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md">Third-party notices and licensing boundaries ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/DevElectrum/grand-anthology">Grand Anthology public source ↗</a></li></ul></section>
    <div class="notice">Unofficial, noncommercial, experimental fan modification. Pokémon names, characters, and related marks belong to their respective owners. No endorsement is implied by upstream contributors or Pokémon rights holders. The illustrated atlas is concept artwork, not an in-game screenshot.</div>
  </div>
</Base>
